    <collectionProcessors>
        <name>Filter_for_Birthdate_and_Phone</name>
        <label>Filter for Birthdate and Phone</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <assignNextValueToReference>currentItem_Filter_for_Birthdate_and_Phone</assignNextValueToReference>
        <collectionProcessorType>FilterCollectionProcessor</collectionProcessorType>
        <collectionReference>Get_Contacts</collectionReference>
        <conditionLogic>formula_evaluation</conditionLogic>
        <connector><targetReference>Set_Result_Count</targetReference></connector>
        <formula>AND(
    OR(ISBLANK({!ESC_Birthdate}), {!currentItem_Filter_for_Birthdate_and_Phone.Birthdate} = {!ESC_Birthdate}),
    OR(ISBLANK({!ESC_Phone}), CONTAINS({!currentItem_Filter_for_Birthdate_and_Phone.Phone}, {!ESC_Phone}))
)</formula>
    </collectionProcessors>
    <description>THROWAWAY Build Step 1 spike (IPOP-47 / IPOP-130). Native-declarative patient search: Name, Date of Birth and Phone inputs, then Get Records on Contact (Name contains), then a Collection Filter for the optional Date of Birth and Phone, then a single-select Data Table. Used to test the search-button refresh pattern, the Data Table search bar and the row cap by hand. Not for the customer build.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
